\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Empirical distribution of the ratio of consecutive eigenvalue spacings in the bulk of the NTK, for $N=64$ points, dimension $D=10$, $M=20$ samples, and $L=2$ layers. The blue curve shows the numerically obtained histogram, while the red curve corresponds to the theoretical GOE prediction (see Equation~\eqref  {eq:goe_ratio_dist}). This result confirms that the NTK, in this configuration, exhibits spacing statistics characteristic of the GOE, illustrating the strong level repulsion expected for real symmetric random matrices.}}{66}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
